<?xml version='1.0' encoding='UTF-8'?>
<D20Rules game-system="D&amp;D4E">
  <!-- These feats describe encounter abilities whose complete power records
       already exist in the private corpus, but omit the corresponding grants.
       Reuse those records rather than duplicating their published text. -->
  <!-- Battle Awareness: the feat power is distinct from the same-named
       fighter utility power (ID_FMP_POWER_1440). -->
  <!-- The feat power's record is named "Battle Awareness Feat" to tell it
       apart from the utility; a feat's power carries the feat's own name. -->
  <AppendNodes internal-id="ID_FMP_POWER_6592" name="Battle Awareness" />
  <AppendNodes internal-id="ID_FMP_FEAT_911">
    <rules>
      <grant name="ID_FMP_POWER_6592" type="Power" />
    </rules>
  </AppendNodes>
  <!-- Path of Destruction (ID_FMP_FEAT_1706) grants its encounter feat power
       under the record name "Path of Destruction (Channel Divinity)", which
       only tells it apart from the unrelated Tharashk Wayfinder daily attack
       of the same name (ID_FMP_POWER_7609, referenced by ID only). The feat's
       power carries the feat's name (owner decision, 2026-10-25). -->
  <AppendNodes internal-id="ID_FMP_POWER_8178" name="Path of Destruction" />
  <!-- Arcane Prodigy retains its existing tier scaling and class metadata. -->
  <AppendNodes internal-id="ID_FMP_FEAT_669">
    <rules>
      <grant name="ID_FMP_POWER_9782" type="Power" />
    </rules>
  </AppendNodes>
  <!-- Blade Initiate: the complete daily feat power ID_FMP_POWER_7691
       ("Swordmage Warding", Display "Feat Power") exists but nothing grants
       it. Its name is the class feature it invokes, not a disambiguated
       variant of the feat's, so it is kept. -->
  <AppendNodes internal-id="ID_FMP_FEAT_650">
    <rules>
      <grant name="ID_FMP_POWER_7691" type="Power" />
    </rules>
  </AppendNodes>

  <!-- Feats (and two Student of the Plague traits) whose text describes a
       limited-use ability the player invokes, with no power record at all.
       Each record is structure for a power card: usage, action, target or
       trigger, written as a concise original summary of the mechanics. No
       published prose is copied (D089); the feat's own description stays the
       full text. The legacy builder showed no power for any of these. A
       triggered ability whose text names no action is "No Action". Each power
       carries the feat's (or trait's) name and is granted by it. The audit
       and classification are in docs/tasks-triage.md, item 8. -->
  <!-- Bravo (ID_FMP_FEAT_1280). -->
  <RulesElement internal-id="ID_4ECB_POWER_BRAVO" name="Bravo" type="Power" source="Dragon Magazine 373">
    <Category>ID_INTERNAL_CATEGORY_ENCOUNTER_USAGE,ID_INTERNAL_CATEGORY_MINOR_ACTION</Category>
    <specific name="Power Usage"> Encounter </specific>
    <specific name="Display"> Feat Power </specific>
    <specific name="Action Type"> Minor Action </specific>
    <specific name="Attack Type"> Personal </specific>
    <specific name="Target"> One creature you can see </specific>
    <specific name="Effect"> The target becomes your prey. You gain a +2 bonus to attack rolls and damage rolls against it until the end of your next turn. </specific>
    <specific name="Special"> The target stays your prey until it drops to 0 hit points or fewer, you end this effect as a free action, or the encounter ends. </specific>
  </RulesElement>
  <AppendNodes internal-id="ID_FMP_FEAT_1280">
    <rules>
      <grant name="ID_4ECB_POWER_BRAVO" type="Power" />
    </rules>
  </AppendNodes>
  <!-- Brawling Warrior (ID_FMP_FEAT_2544). -->
  <RulesElement internal-id="ID_4ECB_POWER_BRAWLING_WARRIOR" name="Brawling Warrior" type="Power" source="Martial Power 2">
    <Category>ID_INTERNAL_CATEGORY_ENCOUNTER_USAGE,ID_INTERNAL_CATEGORY_FREE_ACTION</Category>
    <specific name="Power Usage"> Encounter </specific>
    <specific name="Display"> Feat Power </specific>
    <specific name="Action Type"> Free Action </specific>
    <specific name="Attack Type"> Personal </specific>
    <specific name="Requirement"> Use this power during your turn while wielding a weapon in one hand and nothing in the other. </specific>
    <specific name="Effect"> Choose one: a +1 bonus to an attack roll you just made, or a +1 bonus to AC until the start of your next turn. </specific>
  </RulesElement>
  <AppendNodes internal-id="ID_FMP_FEAT_2544">
    <rules>
      <grant name="ID_4ECB_POWER_BRAWLING_WARRIOR" type="Power" />
    </rules>
  </AppendNodes>
  <!-- Cyclone Warrior (ID_FMP_FEAT_2545). -->
  <RulesElement internal-id="ID_4ECB_POWER_CYCLONE_WARRIOR" name="Cyclone Warrior" type="Power" source="Martial Power 2">
    <Category>ID_INTERNAL_CATEGORY_ENCOUNTER_USAGE,ID_INTERNAL_CATEGORY_FREE_ACTION</Category>
    <specific name="Power Usage"> Encounter </specific>
    <specific name="Display"> Feat Power </specific>
    <specific name="Action Type"> Free Action </specific>
    <specific name="Attack Type"> Personal </specific>
    <specific name="Requirement"> Use this power during your turn while wearing light armor or chainmail and wielding a weapon in each hand. </specific>
    <specific name="Effect"> Until the end of your turn, you gain a +1 bonus to damage rolls with melee attacks and close attacks. The bonus is +2 at 11th level and +3 at 21st level. </specific>
  </RulesElement>
  <AppendNodes internal-id="ID_FMP_FEAT_2545">
    <rules>
      <grant name="ID_4ECB_POWER_CYCLONE_WARRIOR" type="Power" />
    </rules>
  </AppendNodes>
  <!-- Defender of the Wild (ID_FMP_FEAT_671). -->
  <RulesElement internal-id="ID_4ECB_POWER_DEFENDER_OF_THE_WILD" name="Defender of the Wild" type="Power" source="Player's Handbook 2">
    <Category>ID_INTERNAL_CATEGORY_ENCOUNTER_USAGE,ID_INTERNAL_CATEGORY_FREE_ACTION</Category>
    <specific name="Power Usage"> Encounter </specific>
    <specific name="Display"> Feat Power </specific>
    <specific name="Action Type"> Free Action </specific>
    <specific name="Attack Type"> Personal </specific>
    <specific name="Target"> Each enemy adjacent to you </specific>
    <specific name="Effect"> You mark each target until the end of your next turn. </specific>
  </RulesElement>
  <AppendNodes internal-id="ID_FMP_FEAT_671">
    <rules>
      <grant name="ID_4ECB_POWER_DEFENDER_OF_THE_WILD" type="Power" />
    </rules>
  </AppendNodes>
  <!-- Infernal Captain's Pact (ID_FMP_FEAT_1068). -->
  <RulesElement internal-id="ID_4ECB_POWER_INFERNAL_CAPTAINS_PACT" name="Infernal Captain's Pact" type="Power" source="Dragon Magazine 369">
    <Category>ID_INTERNAL_CATEGORY_ENCOUNTER_USAGE,ID_INTERNAL_CATEGORY_MINOR_ACTION</Category>
    <specific name="Power Usage"> Encounter </specific>
    <specific name="Display"> Feat Power </specific>
    <specific name="Action Type"> Minor Action </specific>
    <specific name="Attack Type"> Personal </specific>
    <specific name="Target"> The nearest enemy you can see </specific>
    <specific name="Effect"> The target is under your Infernal Captain's Curse and sheds bright light in a 5-square radius, like a torch. When you hit the target with an attack, choose an ally: the target grants that ally combat advantage for the ally's next attack. </specific>
  </RulesElement>
  <AppendNodes internal-id="ID_FMP_FEAT_1068">
    <rules>
      <grant name="ID_4ECB_POWER_INFERNAL_CAPTAINS_PACT" type="Power" />
    </rules>
  </AppendNodes>
  <!-- Student of the Sword (ID_FMP_FEAT_334). -->
  <RulesElement internal-id="ID_4ECB_POWER_STUDENT_OF_THE_SWORD" name="Student of the Sword" type="Power" source="Player's Handbook">
    <Category>ID_INTERNAL_CATEGORY_ENCOUNTER_USAGE,ID_INTERNAL_CATEGORY_FREE_ACTION</Category>
    <specific name="Power Usage"> Encounter </specific>
    <specific name="Display"> Feat Power </specific>
    <specific name="Action Type"> Free Action </specific>
    <specific name="Attack Type"> Personal </specific>
    <specific name="Effect"> You gain a +1 bonus to your next attack roll with a melee weapon of the category you chose for this feat (one-handed or two-handed). Whether that attack hits or misses, you mark its target until the end of your next turn. </specific>
  </RulesElement>
  <AppendNodes internal-id="ID_FMP_FEAT_334">
    <rules>
      <grant name="ID_4ECB_POWER_STUDENT_OF_THE_SWORD" type="Power" />
    </rules>
  </AppendNodes>
  <!-- Sly Dodge (ID_FMP_FEAT_917). -->
  <RulesElement internal-id="ID_4ECB_POWER_SLY_DODGE" name="Sly Dodge" type="Power" source="Martial Power">
    <Category>ID_INTERNAL_CATEGORY_ENCOUNTER_USAGE,ID_INTERNAL_CATEGORY_NO_ACTION</Category>
    <specific name="Power Usage"> Encounter </specific>
    <specific name="Display"> Feat Power </specific>
    <specific name="Action Type"> No Action </specific>
    <specific name="Attack Type"> Personal </specific>
    <specific name="Trigger"> An enemy makes an opportunity attack against you. </specific>
    <specific name="Effect"> You add your Charisma modifier to your AC against the triggering attack. </specific>
  </RulesElement>
  <AppendNodes internal-id="ID_FMP_FEAT_917">
    <rules>
      <grant name="ID_4ECB_POWER_SLY_DODGE" type="Power" />
    </rules>
  </AppendNodes>
  <!-- Twilight Adept (ID_FMP_FEAT_2549). -->
  <RulesElement internal-id="ID_4ECB_POWER_TWILIGHT_ADEPT" name="Twilight Adept" type="Power" source="Martial Power 2">
    <Category>ID_INTERNAL_CATEGORY_ENCOUNTER_USAGE,ID_INTERNAL_CATEGORY_FREE_ACTION</Category>
    <specific name="Power Usage"> Encounter </specific>
    <specific name="Display"> Feat Power </specific>
    <specific name="Action Type"> Free Action </specific>
    <specific name="Attack Type"> Personal </specific>
    <specific name="Requirement"> Use this power during your turn. </specific>
    <specific name="Effect"> Until the end of your turn, you gain the benefit of the rogue's Cunning Sneak class feature. </specific>
  </RulesElement>
  <AppendNodes internal-id="ID_FMP_FEAT_2549">
    <rules>
      <grant name="ID_4ECB_POWER_TWILIGHT_ADEPT" type="Power" />
    </rules>
  </AppendNodes>
  <!-- Warden's Endurance (ID_FMP_FEAT_1940). -->
  <RulesElement internal-id="ID_4ECB_POWER_WARDENS_ENDURANCE" name="Warden's Endurance" type="Power" source="Primal Power">
    <Category>ID_INTERNAL_CATEGORY_ENCOUNTER_USAGE,ID_INTERNAL_CATEGORY_NO_ACTION</Category>
    <specific name="Power Usage"> Encounter </specific>
    <specific name="Display"> Feat Power </specific>
    <specific name="Action Type"> No Action </specific>
    <specific name="Attack Type"> Personal </specific>
    <specific name="Trigger"> Your turn starts while a save can end an effect on you. </specific>
    <specific name="Effect"> Make a saving throw against one such effect. On a save, it ends immediately and does not affect you this turn. On a failure, you still save against it at the end of your turn. </specific>
  </RulesElement>
  <AppendNodes internal-id="ID_FMP_FEAT_1940">
    <rules>
      <grant name="ID_4ECB_POWER_WARDENS_ENDURANCE" type="Power" />
    </rules>
  </AppendNodes>
  <!-- Wrathful Warrior (ID_FMP_FEAT_2550). -->
  <RulesElement internal-id="ID_4ECB_POWER_WRATHFUL_WARRIOR" name="Wrathful Warrior" type="Power" source="Martial Power 2">
    <Category>ID_INTERNAL_CATEGORY_ENCOUNTER_USAGE,ID_INTERNAL_CATEGORY_NO_ACTION</Category>
    <specific name="Power Usage"> Encounter </specific>
    <specific name="Display"> Feat Power </specific>
    <specific name="Action Type"> No Action </specific>
    <specific name="Attack Type"> Personal </specific>
    <specific name="Trigger"> You are hit by a melee attack or a close attack. </specific>
    <specific name="Effect"> You gain temporary hit points equal to your Constitution modifier. </specific>
  </RulesElement>
  <AppendNodes internal-id="ID_FMP_FEAT_2550">
    <rules>
      <grant name="ID_4ECB_POWER_WRATHFUL_WARRIOR" type="Power" />
    </rules>
  </AppendNodes>
  <!-- Practiced Killer (ID_FMP_FEAT_3615). -->
  <RulesElement internal-id="ID_4ECB_POWER_PRACTICED_KILLER" name="Practiced Killer" type="Power" source="Dragon Magazine 400">
    <Category>ID_INTERNAL_CATEGORY_ENCOUNTER_USAGE,ID_INTERNAL_CATEGORY_NO_ACTION</Category>
    <specific name="Power Usage"> Encounter </specific>
    <specific name="Display"> Feat Power </specific>
    <specific name="Action Type"> No Action </specific>
    <specific name="Attack Type"> Personal </specific>
    <specific name="Trigger"> You hit with a weapon attack using a one-handed weapon, a garrote, a blowgun or a shortbow. </specific>
    <specific name="Effect"> The attack deals 1d8 extra damage: 2d8 at 11th level and 3d8 at 21st level. </specific>
  </RulesElement>
  <AppendNodes internal-id="ID_FMP_FEAT_3615">
    <rules>
      <grant name="ID_4ECB_POWER_PRACTICED_KILLER" type="Power" />
    </rules>
  </AppendNodes>
  <!-- Berserker's Fury (ID_FMP_FEAT_664). -->
  <RulesElement internal-id="ID_4ECB_POWER_BERSERKERS_FURY" name="Berserker's Fury" type="Power" source="Player's Handbook 2">
    <Category>ID_INTERNAL_CATEGORY_DAILY_USAGE,ID_INTERNAL_CATEGORY_FREE_ACTION</Category>
    <specific name="Power Usage"> Daily </specific>
    <specific name="Display"> Feat Power </specific>
    <specific name="Action Type"> Free Action </specific>
    <specific name="Attack Type"> Personal </specific>
    <specific name="Effect"> You gain a +2 bonus to damage rolls until the end of the encounter. </specific>
  </RulesElement>
  <AppendNodes internal-id="ID_FMP_FEAT_664">
    <rules>
      <grant name="ID_4ECB_POWER_BERSERKERS_FURY" type="Power" />
    </rules>
  </AppendNodes>
  <!-- Flamespeed (ID_INTERNAL_CLASS_FEATURE_FLAMESPEED). -->
  <RulesElement internal-id="ID_4ECB_POWER_FLAMESPEED" name="Flamespeed" type="Power" source="Forgotten Realms Player's Guide">
    <Category>ID_INTERNAL_CATEGORY_ENCOUNTER_USAGE,ID_INTERNAL_CATEGORY_MINOR_ACTION</Category>
    <specific name="Power Usage"> Encounter </specific>
    <specific name="Display"> Feat Power </specific>
    <specific name="Action Type"> Minor Action </specific>
    <specific name="Attack Type"> Personal </specific>
    <specific name="Effect"> Until the end of your next turn, you gain a +1 bonus to speed, or a +2 bonus when you charge or run. </specific>
  </RulesElement>
  <AppendNodes internal-id="ID_INTERNAL_CLASS_FEATURE_FLAMESPEED">
    <rules>
      <grant name="ID_4ECB_POWER_FLAMESPEED" type="Power" />
    </rules>
  </AppendNodes>
  <!-- Larger than Life (ID_INTERNAL_CLASS_FEATURE_LARGER_THAN_LIFE). -->
  <RulesElement internal-id="ID_4ECB_POWER_LARGER_THAN_LIFE" name="Larger than Life" type="Power" source="Forgotten Realms Player's Guide">
    <Category>ID_INTERNAL_CATEGORY_DAILY_USAGE,ID_INTERNAL_CATEGORY_FREE_ACTION</Category>
    <specific name="Power Usage"> Daily </specific>
    <specific name="Display"> Feat Power </specific>
    <specific name="Action Type"> Free Action </specific>
    <specific name="Attack Type"> Personal </specific>
    <specific name="Effect"> The reach of an attack you make increases by 1. </specific>
  </RulesElement>
  <AppendNodes internal-id="ID_INTERNAL_CLASS_FEATURE_LARGER_THAN_LIFE">
    <rules>
      <grant name="ID_4ECB_POWER_LARGER_THAN_LIFE" type="Power" />
    </rules>
  </AppendNodes>
  <!-- Secret of Enduring Vigor (ID_FMP_FEAT_2687). -->
  <RulesElement internal-id="ID_4ECB_POWER_SECRET_OF_ENDURING_VIGOR" name="Secret of Enduring Vigor" type="Power" source="Player's Handbook 3">
    <Category>ID_INTERNAL_CATEGORY_DAILY_USAGE,ID_INTERNAL_CATEGORY_IMMEDIATE_INTERRUPT</Category>
    <specific name="Power Usage"> Daily </specific>
    <specific name="Display"> Feat Power </specific>
    <specific name="Action Type"> Immediate Interrupt </specific>
    <specific name="Attack Type"> Personal </specific>
    <specific name="Trigger"> You drop to 0 hit points or fewer. </specific>
    <specific name="Effect"> You spend a healing surge. </specific>
  </RulesElement>
  <AppendNodes internal-id="ID_FMP_FEAT_2687">
    <rules>
      <grant name="ID_4ECB_POWER_SECRET_OF_ENDURING_VIGOR" type="Power" />
    </rules>
  </AppendNodes>
  <!-- Secret of Escape (ID_FMP_FEAT_2662). -->
  <RulesElement internal-id="ID_4ECB_POWER_SECRET_OF_ESCAPE" name="Secret of Escape" type="Power" source="Player's Handbook 3">
    <Category>ID_INTERNAL_CATEGORY_DAILY_USAGE,ID_INTERNAL_CATEGORY_NO_ACTION</Category>
    <specific name="Power Usage"> Daily </specific>
    <specific name="Display"> Feat Power </specific>
    <specific name="Action Type"> No Action </specific>
    <specific name="Attack Type"> Personal </specific>
    <specific name="Trigger"> You drop to 0 hit points or fewer and don't die. </specific>
    <specific name="Effect"> You teleport to a square adjacent to an ally within 10 squares of you. </specific>
  </RulesElement>
  <AppendNodes internal-id="ID_FMP_FEAT_2662">
    <rules>
      <grant name="ID_4ECB_POWER_SECRET_OF_ESCAPE" type="Power" />
    </rules>
  </AppendNodes>
  <!-- Glorious Victory (ID_FMP_FEAT_2203). -->
  <RulesElement internal-id="ID_4ECB_POWER_GLORIOUS_VICTORY" name="Glorious Victory" type="Power" source="Player's Handbook Races: Dragonborn">
    <Category>ID_INTERNAL_CATEGORY_ENCOUNTER_USAGE,ID_INTERNAL_CATEGORY_NO_ACTION</Category>
    <specific name="Power Usage"> Encounter </specific>
    <specific name="Display"> Feat Power </specific>
    <specific name="Action Type"> No Action </specific>
    <specific name="Attack Type"> Personal </specific>
    <specific name="Trigger"> You reduce an enemy to 0 hit points or fewer with an attack. </specific>
    <specific name="Effect"> You can spend a healing surge. </specific>
  </RulesElement>
  <AppendNodes internal-id="ID_FMP_FEAT_2203">
    <rules>
      <grant name="ID_4ECB_POWER_GLORIOUS_VICTORY" type="Power" />
    </rules>
  </AppendNodes>
  <!-- Fast Manifestation (ID_FMP_FEAT_922). -->
  <RulesElement internal-id="ID_4ECB_POWER_FAST_MANIFESTATION" name="Fast Manifestation" type="Power" source="Dragon Magazine 367">
    <Category>ID_INTERNAL_CATEGORY_DAILY_USAGE,ID_INTERNAL_CATEGORY_MINOR_ACTION</Category>
    <specific name="Power Usage"> Daily </specific>
    <specific name="Display"> Feat Power </specific>
    <specific name="Action Type"> Minor Action </specific>
    <specific name="Attack Type"> Personal </specific>
    <specific name="Effect"> You change your elemental manifestation. If you have used the encounter power of your previous manifestation, you can still use the new manifestation's encounter power. </specific>
  </RulesElement>
  <AppendNodes internal-id="ID_FMP_FEAT_922">
    <rules>
      <grant name="ID_4ECB_POWER_FAST_MANIFESTATION" type="Power" />
    </rules>
  </AppendNodes>

  <!-- Far Thought (ID_FMP_FEAT_3176): its only rule granted permanent
       Telepathy vision, but the feat allows telepathy once per day for 5
       minutes. The permanent sense is removed (RemoveNodes <rules /> clears
       the feat's rules; that grant was the only one) and the daily use
       becomes a power card (owner decision, 2026-10-25). The text names no
       action and nothing triggers it, so it is a Free Action. -->
  <RulesElement internal-id="ID_4ECB_POWER_FAR_THOUGHT" name="Far Thought" type="Power" source="Dragon Magazine 389">
    <Category>ID_INTERNAL_CATEGORY_DAILY_USAGE,ID_INTERNAL_CATEGORY_FREE_ACTION</Category>
    <specific name="Power Usage"> Daily </specific>
    <specific name="Display"> Feat Power </specific>
    <specific name="Action Type"> Free Action </specific>
    <specific name="Attack Type"> Personal </specific>
    <specific name="Effect"> For 5 minutes you have telepathy 5, two-way, with creatures you can see that have a language. </specific>
  </RulesElement>
  <RemoveNodes internal-id="ID_FMP_FEAT_3176">
    <rules />
  </RemoveNodes>
  <AppendNodes internal-id="ID_FMP_FEAT_3176">
    <rules>
      <grant name="ID_4ECB_POWER_FAR_THOUGHT" type="Power" />
    </rules>
  </AppendNodes>

  <!-- Power swaps whose power-replace cannot resolve or is missing. Native
       power-replace="GAIN:LOSE" gains the Power named exactly GAIN (name or
       ID) in exchange for an owned power matching category LOSE. Each feat
       had only this rule (or none), so <rules /> is cleared and rewritten. -->
  <!-- Blowgun Expert (ID_FMP_FEAT_1278): "uncanny aim" names no power; the
       blowgun version is "Uncanny Aim (Blowgun)" (ID_FMP_POWER_7356), so it
       is referenced by ID. -->
  <RemoveNodes internal-id="ID_FMP_FEAT_1278">
    <rules />
  </RemoveNodes>
  <AppendNodes internal-id="ID_FMP_FEAT_1278">
    <rules>
      <replace power-replace="ID_FMP_POWER_7356:utility,6+" optional="true" />
    </rules>
  </AppendNodes>
  <!-- Gythka Novice (ID_FMP_FEAT_3212): "Gythka Claw Scoop" is a typo for
       Gythka Claw Swoop (ID_FMP_POWER_12925). The feat swaps a level 3+
       encounter attack power, so LOSE is narrowed from "attack,3+" (which
       also allowed dailies) to "encounter,attack,3+" (D091, the feat's own
       text). -->
  <RemoveNodes internal-id="ID_FMP_FEAT_3212">
    <rules />
  </RemoveNodes>
  <AppendNodes internal-id="ID_FMP_FEAT_3212">
    <rules>
      <replace power-replace="ID_FMP_POWER_12925:encounter,attack,3+" optional="true" />
    </rules>
  </AppendNodes>
  <!-- Disrupting Shot (ID_FMP_FEAT_3631) had no rule: lose a leveled ranger
       encounter attack power, gain Disruptive Shot. The gain is the CBLoader
       ranger copy of the hunter power (ID_FMP_POWER_13588_DISRUPTING_SHOT,
       Level 1, prerequisite this feat), not the hunter class-feature record
       ID_FMP_POWER_13588, whose prerequisite is the Hunter class. The copy
       also stays choosable in a level-1+ ranger encounter slot, as in the
       legacy builder. -->
  <AppendNodes internal-id="ID_FMP_FEAT_3631">
    <rules>
      <replace power-replace="ID_FMP_POWER_13588_DISRUPTING_SHOT:ID_FMP_CLASS_5,encounter,attack,1+" optional="true" />
    </rules>
  </AppendNodes>

</D20Rules>
